#
# One account's statement for a period, in Sutra (reckoner_rules.h RR1),
# one account per row: the closing balance is the opening balance plus
# the period's credits minus its debits, in integer minor units, as a
# camt.053 statement reconciles. credits and debits are totals of one
# direction each, never below 0: they fit 9(18), so a negative or a total
# past 18 digits is a size error, refused; the balances fit s9(18) either
# way. statement.tb says the same in Trebago, which answers to 64 bits:
# past 18 digits the two disagree and the answer is held.
record period-statement
  opening: s9(18)
  credits: 9(18)
  debits: 9(18)
  closing: s9(18)
procedure
  compute closing = opening + credits - debits
  answer closing
